@page "/settings"

<PageTitle>Settings</PageTitle>

<div class="page-shell">
    <section class="hero-card">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Admin</p>
            <h1>Settings</h1>
            <p>Configure the operator experience, onboarding readiness, and the services that power ingestion.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="secondary-button" href="/ingestion">Review ingestion runs</a>
    </section>

    <section class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
            <div class="card-header">
                <h2>Authentication</h2>
                <span class="status-pill status-ready">Configured</span>
            </div>
            <p class="card-body">Login and route protection are wired to the new shell. The demo account remains simple and easy to exercise.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
            <div class="card-header">
                <h2>Ingestion defaults</h2>
                <span class="status-pill status-neutral">Defaults</span>
            </div>
            <p class="card-body">Daily runs, stale-index warnings, and retry backoff values are visible in the shell and ready for the next API integration.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
            <div class="card-header">
                <h2>Observability</h2>
                <span class="status-pill status-warning">Needs attention</span>
            </div>
            <p class="card-body">The workbench surfaces the core health checks that should be expanded once the live ingestion endpoints are connected.</p>
        </article>
    </section>
</div>
